<title>SPAIN: SOCCER-LEADING SCORERS IN THE SPANISH FIRST DIVISION.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-LEADING SCORERS IN THE SPANISH FIRST DIVISION.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading scorers in the Spanish first division after Sunday's matches:  </p>
<p>5  -  Ronaldo (Barcelona)</p>
<p>4  -  Rivaldo (Deportivo Coruna), Romario (Valencia)</p>
<p>3  -  Juan Eduardo Esnaider (Atletico Madrid), Corentine</p>
<p>	 Martins (Deportivo Coruna), Manel Martinez (Logrones),</p>
<p>	 Oli Alvarez (Oviedo), Raul Gonzalez (Real Madrid), Darko</p>
<p>	 Kovacevic (Real Sociedad), Gustavo Poyet (Zaragoza), </p>
<p>	 Gustavo Lopez (Zaragoza), Guilherme (Rayo Vallecano),</p>
<p>	 Luis Enrique Martinez (Real Madrid), Jordi Lardin </p>
<p>	 (Espanyol), Miguel Angel Benitez (Espanyol).</p>
